    description: "Found by the 2026-11-07 docstring staleness audit (dev 4f2feb451b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11072026/review, verify and blind). Corpus impact not measured. CONTAINABLE_KINDS (linkers/containment.py:122) omits constructor, so _may_be_contained rejects it; Java lands instantiates on the class (java.py:3747, :3759); construction.initializer_hops and construction_calls return [] on java and dart fixtures, [__init__ pair] on python. is_initializer already accepts kind constructor (symbol_kinds.py:912-913). Related to, not a duplicate of, WI-sujon. r26, v10."  # f1f5
